19	 * of a continue-as-new chain, so the other axes do not name a stream.
20	 *
21	 * The documented contract: REST fetch FIRST, then attach the transcript WS with
22	 * `after_seq` = the last fetched `store_seq`, so the socket serves only the live
23	 * tail past the fetched history (the server suppresses `store_seq <= after_seq`
24	 * and the console fold also drops persisted duplicates — the splice seam is
25	 * double-covered). An empty list/array is the honest answer for a pre-retention
26	 * run, never an error. Kept out of `client.ts` deliberately: that file is
27	 * already at the house LOC limit.
